    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ConnectionProbeResult.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ConnectionProbeResult.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.ConnectionProbeResult",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ConnectionProbeResult.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">The outcome of <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ProbeConnection(System.Nullable%7bSystem.Int32%7d)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>: whether the controller answered a\ncommand, how long the round trip took, and when it did not answer, why.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.ControllerCommandException",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">A command the controller refused, or answered with a reply the SDK could not read as a value.</p>\n<p></p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">It is raised by the members that answer with the value itself and so have nowhere to report a\nfailure — the typed properties, <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.GetValue(AAMotion.AxisRef%2cAAMotion.eKeyword%2cSystem.Int32)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> — where a 0 is\nindistinguishable from the controller genuinely reporting 0.\n<xref href=\"AAMotion.ISingleAxis.TryRead(AAMotion.eKeyword%2cSystem.Double%40)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>, <xref href=\"AAMotion.ISingleAxis.TryReadArray(AAMotion.eKeyword%2cSystem.Int32%2cSystem.Double%40)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and\n<xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.TryGetValue(AAMotion.AxisRef%2cAAMotion.eKeyword%2cSystem.Double%40%2cSystem.Int32)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> report the same failure as <code>false</code> and never\nthrow. Either way the failed read is recorded in <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.LastReadError\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\nand counted by <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ReadFailures\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>.</p>\n<p></p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"15\">A typed property <b>set</b> the controller refuses raises it as well, with <xref href=\"AAMotion.ControllerCommandException.Command\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>\ncarrying the assignment exactly as sent (<code>ASpeed=1000</code>) — a dropped write leaves the next\nread answering the old value, with nothing at the call site to say so. A failed write is\ndeliberately <b>not</b> recorded in <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.LastReadError\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and not counted\nby <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ReadFailures\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>: both are the read record, by name and by their\nown contract, so a consumer reading them keeps being told about reads and nothing else. There\nis no <code>TrySet</code> — catch this, or subscribe to <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ErrorOccurred\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref>,\nwhich is raised for the refusal as before.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ControllerErrorEventArgs.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ControllerErrorEventArgs.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.ControllerErrorEventArgs",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ControllerErrorEventArgs.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">One error <xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ErrorReported\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> reports: everything\n<xref href=\"AAMotion.MotionController.ErrorOccurred\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> carries, plus which AAMotion member the\napplication called, the axis and parameter the failed command named, where the error came from,\nand when and on which thread it was raised.</p>\n"
    },
