      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.IECAM",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.IECAM.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">The electronic-cam surface: the table registers, and the helpers that fill a table and run it.</p>\n<p></p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.IECAM.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">Its <xref href=\"System.Int32\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> arguments are controller quantities in counts - <code>GenData</code> element\nindices, cycle counts, a master keyword code, and the table entries themselves, which the\ncontroller consumes as counts. Nothing on this surface converts units, so the whole-number\nsignatures are the contract rather than a missing retype.</p>\n"
    },
    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/AAMotion.IGroupAxis.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/AAMotion.IGroupAxis.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.IGroupAxis",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.IGroupAxis.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">IGroupAxis interface definition, used to describe the parameters and states related to the CNC group axes</p>\n<p></p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.IGroupAxis.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"5\">Every CNC segment member takes its arguments in controller counts. A segment is pushed as\n<code>CNCAPushType</code> / <code>CNCAPushParam</code> commands (<code>CNCB</code> on group B) that the Global User\nUnits seam does not scale, so a caller converts\nfrom its own display units first and the whole-number <xref href=\"System.Int32\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> signatures are the\ncontract rather than a missing retype.</p>\n"
    },
