    {
      "type": "ManagedReference",
      "source_relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml",
      "output": {
        ".html": {
          "relative_path": "api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.html"
        }
      },
      "version": "",
      "Uid": null,
      "IsMRef": true,
      "Title": "AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter",
      "Summary": "<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"1\">Parameter type converter - handles type conversion for controller parameters.</p>\n<p sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"3\">Core functionality:</p>\n<ul sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"4\">\n<li sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"4\">The value slot is a <xref href=\"System.Double\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> and holds the parameter's value as the caller sees\nit, including any User Units scaling AAComm has applied to the reply</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"6\">Replies are read as decimal numbers and writes are rendered back with the same invariant\nwire text, so a scaled integral parameter keeps its fraction in both directions</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"8\">A write carries the display value whole; AAComm's transmit seam divides it by the User\nUnits factor and rounds a firmware-integral parameter in controller counts, so rounding\nhappens once, below the scaling, on every transport</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"11\">long: read with a separate command rather than from the slot; the controller's 64-bit\nparameters stay inside +/-2^51, which a double holds exactly</li>\n<li sourcefile=\"api/AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.yml\" sourcestartlinenumber=\"13\">Type detection comes from XML metadata or the cache; use <xref href=\"AAMotion.ParameterTypeConverter.ToInt32Register(System.Double)\" data-throw-if-not-resolved=\"false\"></xref> for\nbit arithmetic on a register-shaped parameter</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
